        "id": 201293,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-08-06T05:43:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think you may be under-estimating the variablility of Spirit Island. &nbsp;I played a game with Ocean's Hungry Grasp and Bringer of Dreams and Nightmares where we were immediately trounced. &nbsp;We didn't make it through the fourth round. &nbsp;Inland filled up, blight filled the island, everything.</p><p>Then I restarted that game using the same spirits, same adversary, same island. &nbsp;And this time we trounced them. &nbsp;I think it went to the fourth round again, but this time in our favor. &nbsp;And two of the lands the invaders explored (Including the surprise stage three land courtesy of Level 3 Prussia) were the same in both games. &nbsp;In fact, the two that were repeated were Jungle and Jungle/Mountain. &nbsp;Which is notable because the two farthest inland corners were Jungles on both boards. &nbsp;And yet in one game I was trounced and in the other I did the trouncing.</p><p>Sure, some pairings are going to be more synergistic than others. &nbsp;But don't assume that you can judge a pairing from a single game.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:29:46.218Z",
